The mission runtime guards for Splinter Faction.

These are the game side of the coilbox mission runtime's adoption contract, items
2 and 3 in docs/mission-runtime.md. They are Splinter Faction's changes to make,
not coilbox's, so they live here as a patch rather than in the game.

Three guards, in two of the game's own gadgets:

1. game_end.lua holds back the game's own ending while a mission is running. The
   file already aliases Spring.GameOver into a local and both call sites go
   through it, so the alias is the only place that needs the check.
2. game_spawn.lua does not spawn a start unit for a team whose mission placed
   its opening units. Guarding SpawnStartUnit covers all four call sites.
3. game_spawn.lua skips the faction and start-spot phases outright when the
   mission owns every team's start, because a mission picked both before the
   game loaded and the pickers would otherwise sit over the first minute of a
   mission that is already playing.

All three are inert in a normal game: GG.CoilboxMission exists only when the
coilbox_mission modoption named a mission the runtime then loaded.

The two files are Splinter Faction's own, under the GNU GPL v2 or later, and
these additions are offered under the same terms.

Apply it to a clone of https://github.com/SplinterFaction/SplinterFaction with:

    git -C <SplinterFaction.sdd> apply <this file>

and undo it with the same command plus -R. scripts/mission-sf-proof.sh checks for
these guards and will apply this patch for you if you pass --apply-guards.

diff --git a/LuaRules/Gadgets/game_end.lua b/LuaRules/Gadgets/game_end.lua
index 0bade32..b7456de 100644
--- a/LuaRules/Gadgets/game_end.lua
+++ b/LuaRules/Gadgets/game_end.lua
@@ -66,7 +66,14 @@ if gadgetHandler:IsSyncedCode() then
 	local GetTeamUnitCount = Spring.GetTeamUnitCount
 	local GetAIInfo = Spring.GetAIInfo
 	local GetTeamLuaAI = Spring.GetTeamLuaAI
-	local GameOver = Spring.GameOver
+	-- Coilbox mission runtime: a mission decides when it is over, so hold back
+	-- the game's own ending while one is running. Both calls below go through
+	-- this local. See missions/runtime.lua.
+	local spGameOver = Spring.GameOver
+	local function GameOver(winners)
+		if GG.CoilboxMission then return end
+		spGameOver(winners)
+	end
 	local AreTeamsAllied = Spring.AreTeamsAllied
 	local GetGameFrame = Spring.GetGameFrame

diff --git a/LuaRules/Gadgets/game_spawn.lua b/LuaRules/Gadgets/game_spawn.lua
index b5ff549..4aead83 100644
--- a/LuaRules/Gadgets/game_spawn.lua
+++ b/LuaRules/Gadgets/game_spawn.lua
@@ -587,6 +587,13 @@ end
 --------------------------------------------------------------------------------

 local function SpawnStartUnit(teamID, spawnX, spawnZ)
+	-- A coilbox mission places this team's opening units itself, and undoing a
+	-- start after the fact is not something the runtime can do safely here:
+	-- game_team_com_ends.lua reads a commander dying as the team dying.
+	if GG.CoilboxMission and GG.CoilboxMission.suppressesStart(teamID) then
+		return
+	end
+
 	local startUnit = GetStartUnit(teamID)
 	if not startUnit or startUnit == "" then return end

@@ -695,6 +702,18 @@ function gadget:GameStart()
 		end
 	end

+	-- A coilbox mission picked the faction and the start position before the game
+	-- loaded, so both phases below have nothing left to ask. Running them anyway
+	-- puts a faction picker and a spot picker over the first minute of a mission
+	-- that is already playing. Going straight to "done" also tells the ledger and
+	-- the survival AI the game is running, which is what they read this param for.
+	if GG.CoilboxMission and GG.CoilboxMission.suppressesEveryStart() then
+		phase = "done"
+		Spring.SetGameRulesParam("phase", "done")
+		Spring.Echo("[Game Spawn] a coilbox mission owns every start, skipping the pre-game phases")
+		return
+	end
+
 	-- Load and partition map spots before broadcasting phase so the game rules
 	-- params are ready when widgets first read them.
 	LoadMapSpots()
